<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Warrior Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 2</h2>Phase 1 confirmed that threat is hardly a concern for the <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> in Wrath of the Lich King Classic thanks to its new and improved toolkit.<br/>On the other hand, a first look at <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> on PTR, and especially the <b>pre-nerf</b> — and in some cases even <i>buffed</i> — <b>hard modes</b> showed that tank damage is greatly increased in the next raid. A welcomed change after a boring stroll in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=3456/naxxramas">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Naxxramas</span></a>, but also a scary prospect when we realize that <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> hits three times harder than <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=16028/patchwerk">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Patchwerk</span></a>, the previous benchmark for DTPS.<br/>
<br/>For this reason, I have reduced the threat skew when comparing items for this phase 2 Best in Slot gear guide to prioritize survivability. The traditional <b>Balanced set</b> still aims for hit and expertise caps for consistency and pull variance, but includes more shared items with the <b>Mitigation set</b> aimed to reduce your chances of death against <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> (25).<br/>
<br/>Keep in mind that gearing your <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> highly depends on your raiding environment. While I may recommend mostly defensive gear sets that will fit the majority of players, only you can know what kind of threat is needed in your raid. If your guild requires a <i>higher threat ceiling</i> to withstand the pressure from high-performing damage dealers, then feel free to mix in threat-oriented items to find the <b>balance</b> between threat and survival that works best for <i>your</i> group. But first, make sure your rotation is on point with this <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve">Rotation and Cooldowns guide</a>!<div class="pad"></div>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>How good is the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-80/conquerors-siegebreaker-plate">Protection Warrior Tier 8 set</a>?</b></div></li>
<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">2 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64933/item-warrior-t8-protection-2p-bonus">Increases the critical strike chance of your Devastate ability by 10%.</a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">4 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64936/item-warrior-t8-protection-4p-bonus">Shield Block also grants you 10% reduction to magical damage taken.</a></div></li></ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The increased critical chances on <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47498/devastate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Devastate</span></a> makes running 2 pieces of T8 very appealing for additional threat and damage, all the while still wearing mitigation-focused items. The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46167">shoulders</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46162">chest</a> are already BiS as standalone items anyway, so the set bonus is a nice... bonus.<br/>
<br/>The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64936">4-piece bonus</a> however is a niche one since it ony reduces magic damage taken. The T8 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46164">gloves</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46169">legs</a> pale in comparison to the ilvl 252 off-sets dropping from hard modes which means unlocking the 4p bonus comes with a substantial stats loss, only worth considering for a handful of encounters with high magic damage burst.</div></li></ul>
