<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-protection-warrior-tank-in-phase-2">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 2</h4>After a disappointing phase 1 with a single noteworthy trinket out of three raids, phase 2 finally brings substantial upgrades to the pre-raid trinkets.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46021/royal-seal-of-king-llane">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Seal of King Llane</span></a> are huge EHP upgrades, paired with decent avoidance on-use that can be used a pseudo defensive cooldowns. They are the best trinkets against both physical and magical damage so real no-brainers for this phase.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45313/furnace-stone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Furnace Stone</span></a> is an okay trinket for raw avoidance if you're a big fan of solo-ing content, but still worse than the trusty <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44063/figurine-monarch-crab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_goldencrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Figurine - Monarch Crab</span></a> for EHP primarily and every other intricate metrics used to calculate survivability. When it comes to mitigating physical damage, it's basically on par with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40257/defenders-code">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defender's Code</span></a>, with a bit more randomness.<br/>
<br/>If you're unlucky with drops in the early weeks of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a>, the recommended trinkets to progress against <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> are <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44063/figurine-monarch-crab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_goldencrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Figurine - Monarch Crab</span></a> and either <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40257/defenders-code">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defender's Code</span></a> or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=37872/lavanthors-talisman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lavanthor's Talisman</span></a>, which on-use effects can help soften the damage taken between major defensive cooldowns and significantly improve your chances of survival compared to purely static trinkets.<div class="pad"></div>
