<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons and Offhands for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 2</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="one-handed-weapons-for-protection-warrior-tank-in-phase-2">One-Handed Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 2</h4>While P1 had barely any tank weapons and most never got the chance to wield <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40402/last-laugh">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_61.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Laugh</span></a> because it was highly contested by <a class="icontiny c6" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/death-knight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>
<span class="c6">s</span>, this time around <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> comes with a plethora of them and from all levels of difficulty.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45442/sorthalis-hammer-of-the-watchers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_91.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sorthalis, Hammer of the Watchers</span></a> is the best of the bunch, with a superior item budget by virtue of its higher item level (how many times did I repeat this in the guide...). It comes with a good socket bonus and secondary stats that make for a perfect offensive weapon to enchant with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59619/enchant-weapon-accuracy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Accuracy</span></a>.<br/>However, it's also a reward from hard mode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=33293/xt-002-deconstructor">
<span class="tinyicontxt">XT-002 Deconstructor</span></a>, considered mathematically impossible before a lot of Ulduar upgrades so this one may take a while to acquire...<br/>
<br/>In the meantime, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45876/shiver">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_90.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shiver</span></a>, from the much more accessible 10-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32845/hodir">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Hodir</span></a> hard mode, is a close second choice. It comes with slightly more mitigation value despite the lower item budget thanks to superior raw stamina and loses only to Sarthalis in the threat department. This would be my go-to pick for a more survivability-oriented alternative weapon to enchant with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=27984/enchant-weapon-mongoose">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Mongoose</span></a> for encounters where tank survival is a primary concern, such as <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a>.<br/>Interestingly enough, none of the tank weapons come with a combination of 3 mitigation secondary stats but all have either hit rating or expertise.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=46860/unrelenting-assault">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_unrelentingassault.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unrelenting Assault</span></a> enthusiasts are out of luck in P2. The only new axes are either PvP weapons or a mediocre 10-man axe, both slow and significant downgrades compared to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40402/last-laugh">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_61.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Laugh</span></a> anyway.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59619/enchant-weapon-accuracy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Accuracy</span></a> (Threat), <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=27984/enchant-weapon-mongoose">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Mongoose</span></a> (Mitigation)<div class="pad"></div>
